N2  - Summary This chapter describes a communications networking protocol architecture that is widely used for the purpose of enabling the timely and reliable transfer of message flows between end users across a communications network. A wireless communications link makes use of a wireless medium, operating at a radio frequency or at other frequency bands. A routing algorithm is employed to determine the best network route to be used by a message flow that is sent from a source node to a destination node. A communications network architecture represents the organization of network system elements and the rules that guide their functions, interactions and inter communications. Communications network elements send messages to each other. A communications networking protocol defines the formats and meanings of such messages, serving to enable their purposeful interactions. The chapter illustrates several networking concepts and methods by considering a package shipping process.
